      "content": "**Troubleshooting Guide: Error 404 - Connectivity Lost on Zenith Smart Hub**\n\n**Step 1: Power Cycle the Device (Recommended Initial Step)**\n\n1.1 Locate the small hole at the bottom of the Zenith Smart Hub, which serves as the device's power reset button.\n1.2 Press and hold the hole for 10 seconds while pressing the \"Power\" button (if your hub has one).\n1.3 Wait for 30 seconds to allow any residual power to discharge from the device.\n1.4 Release the power button and the hole, and wait for an additional 5 seconds to ensure the device has fully reset.\n\n**Step 2: Verify Physical Connections**\n\n2.1 Inspect all cables connected to the Zenith Smart Hub, including the Ethernet cable, power cord, and any other peripherals.\n2.2 Check for signs of physical damage, such as frayed wires, pinched cables, or loose connections.\n2.3 Verify that the Ethernet cable is securely plugged into both the hub and the router/modem.\n2.4 Check the Wi-Fi antenna is undamaged and securely fastened, and that its connectors are clean and free of dust or debris.\n\n**Step 3: Router and",
